course: dictionary
lesson: 6124
title: One word, three meanings
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning, and the words around them tell you which meaning you need. Those words are the context, and they leave clues. Midi is one word with several meanings, so always ask: which meaning fits this sentence?
explain: «Noon and midnight have their own words, midi and minuit.» The word next to minuit tells you midi means noon, the middle of the day. Check by putting your meaning into the sentence: «Noon and midnight have their own words, noon and minuit» still makes sense, so you are right.
explain: Music and fashion use midi in other ways. A «midi skirt» reaches the middle of the lower leg, so it sits between a mini and a maxi. A MIDI keyboard sends music notes to a computer. The capitals stand for Musical Instrument Digital Interface, but the context tells you which meaning is meant.
fact: Midi has three main meanings: a skirt or dress, a music system, and a French word for noon or south.
fact: A midi is a skirt or dress that reaches the middle of the lower leg.
fact: MIDI stands for Musical Instrument Digital Interface, a way for electronic instruments and computers to send music notes to each other.
fact: «Midi» is French for noon, as in «à midi» (at noon), and also for south, as in «le Midi» (the south of France).
fact: The «Canal du Midi» in southern France, built between 1666 and 1681, links the Mediterranean to the River Garonne, so boats could avoid sailing all the way round Spain and Portugal.
exercise: In French lessons, «à midi» means at what time? | At six in the morning | *At noon | In the evening | At midnight
exercise: A girl asks for a «midi skirt». What is a midi skirt? | A pair of trousers | A long skirt that touches the floor | A very short skirt that stops above the knee | *A skirt that reaches the middle of the lower leg
exercise: A musician says, «My MIDI keyboard plays sounds through the computer.» What do the capital letters MIDI stand for? | Mini Instrument Digital Idea | *Musical Instrument Digital Interface | Midday Instrument Data Input | Music in the Daytime Interval
test: «Noon and midnight have their own words, midi and minuit.» In this sentence, what does minuit mean? | Midday meal | *Midnight | Noon | Afternoon
test: «Le midi» is a name used in France. In this name, what does midi mean? | A skirt | Noon | *The south | A music note
exam: Jayden says midi always means midday. What is the best answer? | *No, it can also mean the south of France, a skirt, or a music system | Yes, midi always means midday and nothing else | No, midi means midnight | Yes, but only in music lessons
